  body: "# Family membership during hospital admission\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured hospital
    guidance asks whether a patient remains a member of the family and routes that question to the separate
    family-membership chapter.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe listed contexts include a lone parent,
    a couple, a polygamous marriage and a child or young person. Neither a hospital admission nor a shared
    address alone resolves family membership. The continuation of DMG 24097 is on PDF page 26; chapter
    22 and any current benefit-specific consequences require separate examination.\n\n## Inspected source
    passages\n\n- [DMG 24097, PDF page 25](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5e9f006886650c031ce2c41b/dmgch24.pdf#page=25)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 24: Special cases.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch24`: PDF SHA-256 `2827c11c3ce95e852073142524e0410c6534f7bf140d885be18cad09f6ece98a`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `91863ddf195bf30158383f17cb2653f1ba498551a695c8ec0ba1e138d00a222c`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-applicable-amount
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The hospital section separately considers effects on a claimant’s applicable amount
      when the claimant or a family member is a patient; the dated conditions are retained as
      context, not an automated withdrawal instruction.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch24/0027
      quote: "24108   The normal applicable amount of a claimant may be affected when the claimant or
        a\n        member of his family has been a patient for a continuous period of more than 52\n \
        \       weeks. At this point the DM should consider withdrawing1 any\n\n        1.    HPP\n\n\
        \        2.    DP\n\n        3.    EDP\n\n        4.    DCP.\n\n        Note: But the claimant
        will not normally be able to satisfy all the conditions for JSA\n        (see DMG 24106), and
        may need to claim IS or another appropriate benefit, for\n        example IB.\n              \
        \ 1 JSA Regs, Sch 1, para 12(5), 13(2), 15A(2), 16(2); IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 2, para 10(6), 11(2),
        13A(2), 14(2)"
      locator: DMG 24108
